WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.680
Six unapproved peptides can be compounded in U.S. pharmacies without an FDA safety finding. This is peptides weekly, episode 8. Education and evidence, never dosing advice. After that enforcement shift, a pharmacies November plan, then what ordinary clinics and insurance records show for an oral glp-1 peptide, and why most peptides are still injected. Health and human services in a late October regulatory action, rather than any clinical trial, said it will not go after state license

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:35.280
pharmacies, federal facilities, or license physicians who compound six peptides, the Food

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.420
and Drug Administration has never approved.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:47.420
Bio-exconemy names them as BPC157, Epitalon, KPV, MOTSC, semax, and TB500.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:52.040
The same set in FDA Advisory Committee recommended for compounding in July.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:56.580
The notice does not approve those drugs and does not find them safe or effective.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:01.940
It does ask for preliminary identity and quality standards, and officials say the point

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:05.460
is to pull patients off research use only products sold online.

00:01:06.425 --> 00:01:12.745
Democratic dates the announcement October 28, 2026, signed by Secretary Robert F. Kennedy

00:01:12.745 --> 00:01:17.665
Jr., and describes peptides there as short amino acid chains that can be injected.

00:01:18.225 --> 00:01:22.145
The FDA had already restricted these substances in 2023.

00:01:22.145 --> 00:01:27.805
Lee Rosebush, who chairs the American Academy of Peptide Medicine, framed the change as

00:01:27.805 --> 00:01:31.745
a path out of gray and black markets and into physician-supervised care.

00:01:32.405 --> 00:01:37.545
Fred Mills, chief policy officer for Americans for Safe and Effective Medicines, warned

00:01:37.545 --> 00:01:39.765
against using consumers as test subjects.

00:01:40.713 --> 00:01:45.953
The FDA's Center for Drug Evaluation and Research had already opposed that July recommendation,

00:01:46.413 --> 00:01:51.553
and that opposition is a regulator's scientific judgment, not a result from people in a trial.

00:01:51.553 --> 00:01:57.493
Bio-exconemy reports the drug center called the peptides poorly characterized, with limited

00:01:57.493 --> 00:02:04.033
safety data, immunogenicity concerns, impurity risks, and uncertain dosing. A decision not

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:09.253
to enforce does not withdraw those objections, and it does not turn the 6 into approved medicines.

00:02:10.416 --> 00:02:15.796
Data meds AI in a company announcement rather than a study, said its pharmacy subsidiary

00:02:15.796 --> 00:02:20.796
Correctsa Health now has a supply agreement for bulk drug substance and active ingredient for

00:02:20.796 --> 00:02:26.096
those same six and that corrects a pharmacy intends to start dispensing compounded prescriptions

00:02:26.096 --> 00:02:32.056
in November 2026. Yahoo Finance reports the company stating outright that the peptides

00:02:32.056 --> 00:02:38.896
are not FDA approved and have not been evaluated by the FDA for safety or efficacy. The firm says

00:02:38.896 --> 00:02:44.076
it will use a mobile app called HealthLives here to collect and report safety data under the

00:02:44.076 --> 00:02:49.556
enforcement discretion policy published in the Federal Register on October 30th, 2026.

00:02:49.556 --> 00:02:56.276
Interim COCEO Gerald Commission cast that as a license-farmacy alternative to unregulated

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:58.576
research use only products sold online.

00:02:59.485 --> 00:03:05.105
Oral semaglutide in a retrospective real-world study, rather than a randomized trial, was

00:03:05.105 --> 00:03:11.265
followed in 232 adults with type 2 diabetes, who started it at one Italian diabetes clinic.

00:03:11.805 --> 00:03:19.005
Over 24 months, HBA1C fell by 0.8 percentage points, a drop the author's called significant

00:03:19.005 --> 00:03:21.445
in diabetes, obesity, and metabolism.

00:03:22.125 --> 00:03:26.565
The same observational follow-up describes sustained improvements in blood sugar control,

00:03:27.025 --> 00:03:31.725
body weight and lipids, preserved kidney function, and high persistence on treatment.

00:03:32.425 --> 00:03:34.025
People were not randomly assigned,

00:03:34.265 --> 00:03:38.505
so a before and after shift cannot by itself prove the tablet caused every change.

00:03:39.531 --> 00:03:43.371
A separate observational claim study, again not a randomized trial,

00:03:43.371 --> 00:03:49.211
hospital, compared new users of oral semi-glutide, who had type 2 diabetes and atherosclerotic

00:03:49.211 --> 00:03:54.291
cardiovascular disease, with people starting other non-insulin glucose-lowering drugs.

00:03:54.891 --> 00:04:03.911
Among 10,878 oral semi-glutide users and 28,639 comparators, the tablet group had a 17%

00:04:03.911 --> 00:04:10.431
lower risk of 3-point major adverse cardiovascular events, and a 21% lower risk of a modified

00:04:10.431 --> 00:04:11.491
3-point version.

00:04:11.491 --> 00:04:19.951
Set against 7,218 matched new users of DPP-4 inhibitors, another 7,218 oral

00:04:19.951 --> 00:04:26.431
semi-glutide users had 22% and 24% lower risks of those two outcomes. Set

00:04:26.431 --> 00:04:36.451
against 21,572 SGLT-2 inhibitor users, 7,491 oral semi-glutide users had 21%

00:04:36.451 --> 00:04:42.471
and 22% lower risks. The authors also reported significantly lower risks of broader cardiovascular

00:04:42.471 --> 00:04:48.031
composites, ischemic stroke and death from any cause versus the mixed comparator group.

00:04:48.791 --> 00:04:52.011
Billing record associations are not proof the tablet caused the gap.

00:04:53.115 --> 00:04:57.735
Shilpa Medicare is putting roughly $50 million into peptide manufacturing at its

00:04:57.735 --> 00:05:04.135
right-cher site in India. Bioprocess International Reports, adding solid-phase synthesis aimed at

00:05:04.135 --> 00:05:10.015
GLP1 and other therapeutic peptides, with commercial scale output targeted for 2028.

00:05:10.655 --> 00:05:15.555
The same report says Phil finish is a tighter bottleneck than making the peptide chain, which

00:05:15.555 --> 00:05:20.095
is why some buyers have been locking multi-year supply contracts instead of waiting only on

00:05:20.095 --> 00:05:20.795
new reactors.

00:05:21.515 --> 00:05:26.035
Boxing insider reports that license fighters still cannot use the six peptides that just

00:05:26.035 --> 00:05:28.255
received a US compounding green light.

00:05:28.255 --> 00:05:34.445
Oral semaglutide is this week's spotlight, a GLP-1 peptide built so a fraction of it

00:05:34.445 --> 00:05:37.005
can cross the stomach instead of going in through a needle.

00:05:37.605 --> 00:05:42.725
Most peptide drugs are injected because a peptide is a short chain of amino acids, and the

00:05:42.725 --> 00:05:44.925
gut is designed to cut chains like that apart.

00:05:45.485 --> 00:05:50.645
An injection skips that digestion, getting a peptide into a tablet has to solve two problems

00:05:50.645 --> 00:05:54.805
together, survive the gut, and cross the gut wall in an amount that matters.

00:05:54.805 --> 00:06:01.525
A 2016 review looked at more than 250 intestinal permeation enhancers tested in intestinal

00:06:01.525 --> 00:06:06.665
delivery models, mostly preclinical work, and stressed that enhancer and peptide have

00:06:06.665 --> 00:06:10.725
to show up together at the small intestinal lining in a high enough concentration.

00:06:11.305 --> 00:06:14.645
Some proprietary enhancer systems have reached clinical trials.

00:06:15.145 --> 00:06:17.765
That paper is not a trial of one approved tablet.

00:06:18.205 --> 00:06:23.745
A companion 2016 review of lipid nanocarriers for oral peptides and proteins is an overview

00:06:23.745 --> 00:06:29.525
review of design choices, particle size, surface charge, how much drug is loaded, how fast

00:06:29.525 --> 00:06:33.725
it comes out, and how those choices change the gut trip and later drug levels.

00:06:34.165 --> 00:06:38.465
It does not show that a lipid particle makes every peptide work by mouth and people.

00:06:39.185 --> 00:06:42.665
Semaglutide is a glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor agonist.

00:06:43.105 --> 00:06:48.545
A 2019 review describes that injected class as highly effective at lowering hemoglobin

00:06:48.545 --> 00:06:55.465
A1C, and helping weight loss, and says four injected agents, Alba Glutide, Lyra Glutide,

00:06:56.065 --> 00:07:00.265
Dula Glutide, and Semaglutide also have cardio protective effects.

00:07:00.965 --> 00:07:05.305
The same review says the need for shots is a major reason the class has been underused.

00:07:05.885 --> 00:07:10.785
The oral version pairs Semaglutide with six unapproved peptides can be compounded in

00:07:10.785 --> 00:07:13.485
US pharmacies without an FDA safety finding.

00:07:13.485 --> 00:07:19.185
This is peptides weekly, episode 8, education and evidence, never-dosing advice.

